diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117541.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117541.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This PR allows API users to bind lambdas as member methods in classes used by the engine. This is a proof of concept for the C++ bindings more than anything. Albeit this might sound pointless for the engine, but this is needed by godot-cpp and in case you embed the engine.\r\n\r\nAn example would be the following.\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nvoid Sample::_bind_methods() {\r\n  ClassDB::bind_method(godot::D_METHOD(\"test\"), [](const Sample &s) { return s.test(); });\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nAs seen in this godotengine/godot-proposals#14485 proposal issue.\r\n\r\n> [!NOTE]\r\n> This is intended for discussing the implementation within the engine and the C++ bindings. It's not yet the formal PR as I'd like to see feedback from reviewers before that.\r\n\r\n* *Bugsquad edit, closes: godotengine/godot-proposals#14485*\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117541/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":0,"-1":2,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":2,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117541/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}